{"id":"mahabharata-3-187","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":187,"title":"सप्ताशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 187 · The child reveals himself as Narayana","summary":{"en":"The divine child declares himself Narayana, source and end of all beings, who sleeps on the waters and is born in age after age to restore dharma. Markandeya tells the Pandavas that this very god is Krishna, their kinsman, and bids them take refuge in him.","kn":"ದಿವ್ಯಶಿಶುವು ತಾನು ಸರ್ವಭೂತಗಳ ಉತ್ಪತ್ತಿ ಲಯಸ್ಥಾನನಾದ, ನೀರಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಶಯನಿಸುವ, ಯುಗಯುಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಧರ್ಮಸ್ಥಾಪನೆಗಾಗಿ ಅವತರಿಸುವ ನಾರಾಯಣನೆಂದು ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆ ದೇವನೇ ನಿಮ್ಮ ಬಂಧು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣ, ಅವನಿಗೆ ಶರಣಾಗಿರಿ ಎಂದು ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"दिव्य बालक स्वयं को नारायण घोषित करता है, जो सब प्राणियों के उद्गम और अन्त हैं, जल पर शयन करते हैं और युग-युग में धर्म की स्थापना के लिए जन्म लेते हैं। मार्कण्डेय पाण्डवों से कहते हैं कि वही देव उनके बन्धु श्रीकृष्ण हैं, और उनकी शरण लेने को कहते हैं।","te":"దివ్యశిశువు తాను సర్వభూతాల ఉత్పత్తి లయస్థానమైన, నీటిపై శయనించే, యుగయుగాన ధర్మస్థాపన కోసం అవతరించే నారాయణుడనని ప్రకటిస్తాడు. ఆ దేవుడే మీ బంధువు శ్రీకృష్ణుడని, ఆయనను శరణు పొందమని మార్కండేయుడు పాండవులకు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"தெய்வக் குழந்தை தான் எல்லா உயிர்களின் தோற்றமும் முடிவுமான, நீரில் துயிலும், யுகந்தோறும் அறத்தை நிலைநாட்டப் பிறக்கும் நாராயணன் என்று அறிவிக்கிறது. அந்தத் தெய்வமே உங்கள் உறவினரான ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர், அவரிடம் அடைக்கலம் புகுங்கள் என்று மார்க்கண்டேயர் பாண்டவர்களிடம் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"ദിവ്യശിശു താൻ നാരായണനാണെന്ന് വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു: സകല ജീവികളുടെയും ഉത്ഭവവും അന്ത്യവുമായ, ജലത്തിൽ ശയിക്കുന്ന, ധർമ്മം പുനഃസ്ഥാപിക്കാൻ യുഗംതോറും അവതരിക്കുന്നവൻ. ഇതേ ദൈവമാണ് തങ്ങളുടെ ബന്ധുവായ കൃഷ്ണനെന്നും, അദ്ദേഹത്തിൽ അഭയം തേടണമെന്നും മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ പാണ്ഡവരോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.187; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"देव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The god said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कामं देवापि मां विप्र न विजानन्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nत्वत्प्रीत्या तु प्रवक्ष्यामि यथेदं विसृजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the gods do not truly know me, brahmin, but out of affection for you I will explain how I send forth this world."}},{"n":2,"text":"पितृभक्तोऽसि विप्रर्षे मां चैव शरणं गतः ।\nअतो दृष्टोऽस्मि ते साक्षाद्ब्रह्मचर्यं च ते महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are devoted to your father and have come to me for refuge, sage, so you now see me directly, and your celibacy is great."}},{"n":3,"text":"आपो नारा इति प्रोक्ताः संज्ञानाम कृतं मया ।\nतेन नारायणोऽस्म्युक्तो मम तद्ध्ययनं सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The waters are called \"nara\", a name I gave them myself, and since they are my constant resting place I am called Narayana."}},{"n":4,"text":"अहं नारायणो नाम प्रभवः शाश्वतोऽव्ययः ।\nविधाता सर्वभूतानां संहर्ता च द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Narayana, the eternal, imperishable source, the creator of all beings and also their destroyer, best of brahmins."}},{"n":5,"text":"अहं विष्णुरहं ब्रह्मा शक्रश्चाहं सुराधिपः ।\nअहं वैश्रवणो राजा यमः प्रेताधिपस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Vishnu, I am Brahma, I am Indra, lord of the gods; I am King Kubera and also Yama, lord of the departed."}},{"n":6,"text":"अहं शिवश्च सोमश्च कश्यपश्च प्रजापतिः ।\nअहं धाता विधाता च यज्ञश्चाहं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Shiva and Soma and the progenitor Kashyapa; I am the sustainer and the ordainer, and I am the sacrifice itself, best of brahmins."}},{"n":7,"text":"अग्निरास्यं क्षितिः पादौ चन्द्रादित्यौ च लोचने ।\nसदिशं च नभः कायो वायुर्मनसि मे स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire is my mouth, the earth my feet, the moon and sun my eyes; the sky with its directions is my body, and the wind dwells in my mind."}},{"n":8,"text":"मया क्रतुशतैरिष्टं बहुभिः स्वाप्तदक्षिणैः ।\nयजन्ते वेदविदुषो मां देवयजने स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have performed hundreds of sacrifices with ample fees, and Veda-knowers worship me as I stand at the place of worship."}},{"n":9,"text":"पृथिव्यां क्षत्रियेन्द्राश्च पार्थिवाः स्वर्गकाङ्क्षिणः ।\nयजन्ते मां तथा वैश्याः स्वर्गलोकजिगीषवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warrior kings on earth who long for heaven worship me, and so do merchants who seek to win the heavenly world."}},{"n":10,"text":"चतुःसमुद्रपर्यन्तां मेरुमन्दरभूषणाम् ।\nशेषो भूत्वाहमेवैतां धारयामि वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Shesha I hold up this earth, bounded by four oceans and adorned with Meru and Mandara."}},{"n":11,"text":"वाराहं रूपमास्थाय मयेयं जगती पुरा ।\nमज्जमाना जले विप्र वीर्येणासीत्समुद्धृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the form of a boar, long ago I lifted this world by my might when it was sinking in the waters, brahmin."}},{"n":12,"text":"अग्निश्च वडवावक्त्रो भूत्वाहं द्विजसत्तम ।\nपिबाम्यपः समाविद्धास्ताश्चैव विसृजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Becoming the fire with a mare's mouth, best of brahmins, I drink the churned waters and then release them again."}},{"n":13,"text":"ब्रह्म वक्त्रं भुजौ क्षत्रमूरू मे संश्रिता विशः ।\nपादौ शूद्रा भजन्ते मे विक्रमेण क्रमेण च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins are my mouth, warriors my arms, merchants rest on my thighs, and servants attend my feet with their strength and in due order."}},{"n":14,"text":"ऋग्वेदः सामवेदश्च यजुर्वेदोऽप्यथर्वणः ।\nमत्तः प्रादुर्भवन्त्येते मामेव प्रविशन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Rig, Sama, Yajur and Atharva Vedas arise from me and enter into me again."}},{"n":15,"text":"यतयः शान्तिपरमा यतात्मानो मुमुक्षवः ।\nकामक्रोधद्वेषमुक्ता निःसङ्गा वीतकल्मषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetics who seek peace above all, self-controlled and wishing for liberation, free of desire, anger and hatred, unattached and sinless,"}},{"n":16,"text":"सत्त्वस्था निरहंकारा नित्यमध्यात्मकोविदाः ।\nमामेव सततं विप्राश्चिन्तयन्त उपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"firm in goodness, free of ego and ever skilled in knowledge of the self, brahmins who always meditate on me alone, worship me."}},{"n":17,"text":"अहं संवर्तको ज्योतिरहं संवर्तको यमः ।\nअहं संवर्तकः सूर्यो अहं संवर्तकोऽनिलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the fire of dissolution, I am the Death of dissolution, I am the sun of dissolution, and I am the wind of dissolution."}},{"n":18,"text":"तारारूपाणि दृश्यन्ते यान्येतानि नभस्तले ।\nमम रूपाण्यथैतानि विद्धि त्वं द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"These forms of stars you see across the sky, know them, best of brahmins, to be my forms."}},{"n":19,"text":"रत्नाकराः समुद्राश्च सर्व एव चतुर्दिशम् ।\nवसनं शयनं चैव निलयं चैव विद्धि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know that the oceans, the jewel-mines and all the four directions are my clothing, my bed and my dwelling."}},{"n":20,"text":"कामं क्रोधं च हर्षं च भयं मोहं तथैव च ।\nममैव विद्धि रूपाणि सर्वाण्येतानि सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Desire, anger, joy, fear and delusion as well, good sage, know all these to be my forms."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्राप्नुवन्ति नरा विप्र यत्कृत्वा कर्मशोभनम् ।\nसत्यं दानं तपश्चोग्रमहिंसा चैव जन्तुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The truth, charity, fierce austerity and non-violence toward creatures by which people attain good results, brahmin,"}},{"n":22,"text":"मद्विधानेन विहिता मम देहविहारिणः ।\nमयाभिभूतविज्ञाना विचेष्टन्ते न कामतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"are ordained by my arrangement for those who move within my body; their understanding overpowered by me, they act and do not act by their own desire."}},{"n":23,"text":"सम्यग्वेदमधीयाना यजन्तो विविधैर्मखैः ।\nशान्तात्मानो जितक्रोधाः प्राप्नुवन्ति द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins who study the Veda properly, offer many kinds of sacrifice, and are calm and free of anger attain this."}},{"n":24,"text":"प्राप्तुं न शक्यो यो विद्वन्नरैर्दुष्कृतकर्मभिः ।\nलोभाभिभूतैः कृपणैरनार्यैरकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That which cannot be reached by evil-doers, by the greedy, the miserly, the ignoble and the unrestrained, learned one,"}},{"n":25,"text":"तं मां महाफलं विद्धि पदं सुकृतकर्मणः ।\nदुष्प्रापं विप्रमूढानां मार्गं योगैर्निषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"know me to be that great reward, the state of the righteous, hard to reach for the deluded, the path pursued through yoga."}},{"n":26,"text":"यदा यदा च धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति सत्तम ।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whenever righteousness declines, good sage, and unrighteousness rises, I create myself."}},{"n":27,"text":"दैत्या हिंसानुरक्ताश्च अवध्याः सुरसत्तमैः ।\nराक्षसाश्चापि लोकेऽस्मिन्यदोत्पत्स्यन्ति दारुणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When demons devoted to violence, whom the best of gods cannot kill, and fierce demons are born in this world,"}},{"n":28,"text":"तदाहं संप्रसूयामि गृहेषु शुभकर्मणाम् ।\nप्रविष्टो मानुषं देहं सर्वं प्रशमयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"then I am born in the homes of those of good deeds, and entering a human body I put everything to rest."}},{"n":29,"text":"सृष्ट्वा देवमनुष्यांश्च गन्धर्वोरगराक्षसान् ।\nस्थावराणि च भूतानि संहराम्यात्ममायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having created gods, humans, gandharvas, serpents and demons, and the immovable beings, I withdraw them again by my own power of illusion."}},{"n":30,"text":"कर्मकाले पुनर्देहमनुचिन्त्य सृजाम्यहम् ।\nप्रविश्य मानुषं देहं मर्यादाबन्धकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the time of action I think of my body again and send it forth, entering a human form for the sake of upholding the bounds of order."}},{"n":31,"text":"श्वेतः कृतयुगे वर्णः पीतस्त्रेतायुगे मम ।\nरक्तो द्वापरमासाद्य कृष्णः कलियुगे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Krita age my colour is white, in the Treta yellow, in the Dvapara I take red, and in the Kali age black."}},{"n":32,"text":"त्रयो भागा ह्यधर्मस्य तस्मिन्काले भवन्त्युत ।\nअन्तकाले च संप्राप्ते कालो भूत्वातिदारुणः ।\nत्रैलोक्यं नाशयाम्येकः कृत्स्नं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that time three parts of unrighteousness prevail, and when the end arrives I become terrible Time and alone destroy the three worlds, all that moves and stands still."}},{"n":33,"text":"अहं त्रिवर्त्मा सर्वात्मा सर्वलोकसुखावहः ।\nअभिभूः सर्वगोऽनन्तो हृषीकेश उरुक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the one of three paths, the self of all, the bringer of joy to all worlds, the all-surpassing, all-pervading, infinite Hrishikesha of wide strides."}},{"n":34,"text":"कालचक्रं नयाम्येको ब्रह्मन्नहमरूपि वै ।\nशमनं सर्वभूतानां सर्वलोककृतोद्यमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alone, formless, I turn the wheel of time, brahmin, which brings an end to all beings and sets all the worlds in motion."}},{"n":35,"text":"एवं प्रणिहितः सम्यङ्मयात्मा मुनिसत्तम ।\nसर्वभूतेषु विप्रेन्द्र न च मां वेत्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, best of sages, I am well placed in all beings, best of brahmins, yet no one knows me."}},{"n":36,"text":"यच्च किंचित्त्वया प्राप्तं मयि क्लेशात्मकं द्विज ।\nसुखोदयाय तत्सर्वं श्रेयसे च तवानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever hardship you suffered in me, brahmin, was all for the rise of your happiness and for your good, sinless one."}},{"n":37,"text":"यच्च किंचित्त्वया लोके दृष्टं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nविहितः सर्वथैवासौ ममात्मा मुनिसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever moving or unmoving thing you have seen in the world, best of sages, was all arranged as my own self."}},{"n":38,"text":"अर्धं मम शरीरस्य सर्वलोकपितामहः ।\nअहं नारायणो नाम शङ्खचक्रगदाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Half of my body is Brahma, grandfather of all the worlds; I am Narayana, bearing the conch, discus and mace."}},{"n":39,"text":"यावद्युगानां विप्रर्षे सहस्रपरिवर्तनम् ।\nतावत्स्वपिमि विश्वात्मा सर्वलोकपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For as long as a thousand cycles of the ages turn, brahmin sage, so long do I, the self of the universe, sleep, together with the grandfather of all worlds."}},{"n":40,"text":"एवं सर्वमहं कालमिहासे मुनिसत्तम ।\nअशिशुः शिशुरूपेण यावद्ब्रह्मा न बुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, best of sages, all that time I remain here as a child, though no child, until Brahma wakes."}},{"n":41,"text":"मया च विप्र दत्तोऽयं वरस्ते ब्रह्मरूपिणा ।\nअसकृत्परितुष्टेन विप्रर्षिगणपूजित ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I, in the form of Brahma, pleased again and again, gave you this boon, brahmin, honoured by the company of sages."}},{"n":42,"text":"सर्वमेकार्णवं दृष्ट्वा नष्टं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nविक्लवोऽसि मया ज्ञातस्ततस्ते दर्शितं जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing everything one ocean, with all moving and unmoving things lost, you were bewildered; I understood this, and so I showed you the world."}},{"n":43,"text":"अभ्यन्तरं शरीरस्य प्रविष्टोऽसि यदा मम ।\nदृष्ट्वा लोकं समस्तं च विस्मितो नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you entered inside my body and saw the whole world, you were amazed and did not understand."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततोऽसि वक्त्राद्विप्रर्षे द्रुतं निःसारितो मया ।\nआख्यातस्ते मया चात्मा दुर्ज्ञेयोऽपि सुरासुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I quickly brought you out through my mouth, sage, and told you of myself, though I am hard to know even for gods and demons."}},{"n":45,"text":"यावत्स भगवान्ब्रह्मा न बुध्यति महातपाः ।\nतावत्त्वमिह विप्रर्षे विश्रब्धश्चर वै सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Until the blessed, greatly ascetic Brahma wakes, sage, you may wander here at ease and in comfort."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततो विबुद्धे तस्मिंस्तु सर्वलोकपितामहे ।\nएकीभूतो हि स्रक्ष्यामि शरीराद्द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when that grandfather of all the worlds has awakened, I will merge into one with him and send forth from my body"}},{"n":47,"text":"आकाशं पृथिवीं ज्योतिर्वायुं सलिलमेव च ।\nलोके यच्च भवेच्छेषमिह स्थावरजङ्गमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the sky, the earth, fire, wind and water, and whatever else remains in the world of moving and unmoving things."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":48,"text":"इत्युक्त्वान्तर्हितस्तात स देवः परमाद्भुतः ।\nप्रजाश्चेमाः प्रपश्यामि विचित्रा बहुधाकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus, dear king, that wonderfully marvellous god vanished, and I saw these many varied creatures, made in many forms."}},{"n":49,"text":"एतद्दृष्टं मया राजंस्तस्मिन्प्राप्ते युगक्षये ।\nआश्चर्यं भरतश्रेष्ठ सर्वधर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is what I saw, king, when the end of the age arrived, a wonder, best of the Bharatas and foremost among upholders of dharma."}},{"n":50,"text":"यः स देवो मया दृष्टः पुरा पद्मनिभेक्षणः ।\nस एष पुरुषव्याघ्र संबन्धी ते जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That lotus-eyed god I saw long ago, tiger among men, is this Janardana, your kinsman."}},{"n":51,"text":"अस्यैव वरदानाद्धि स्मृतिर्न प्रजहाति माम् ।\nदीर्घमायुश्च कौन्तेय स्वच्छन्दमरणं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is by his boon that memory does not leave me, and that I have long life and death at my own choosing, son of Kunti."}},{"n":52,"text":"स एष कृष्णो वार्ष्णेयः पुराणपुरुषो विभुः ।\nआस्ते हरिरचिन्त्यात्मा क्रीडन्निव महाभुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is Krishna of the Vrishnis, the ancient Person, the all-pervading Hari of inconceivable nature, mighty-armed, who stays here as if at play."}},{"n":53,"text":"एष धाता विधाता च संहर्ता चैव सात्वतः ।\nश्रीवत्सवक्षा गोविन्दः प्रजापतिपतिः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the sustainer, the ordainer and also the destroyer, the Satvata Govinda with the Shrivatsa on his chest, lord and master of the progenitors."}},{"n":54,"text":"दृष्ट्वेमं वृष्णिशार्दूलं स्मृतिर्मामियमागता ।\nआदिदेवमजं विष्णुं पुरुषं पीतवाससम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing this tiger of the Vrishnis, that memory has come back to me of the primal god, unborn Vishnu, the Person in yellow garments."}},{"n":55,"text":"सर्वेषामेव भूतानां पिता माता च माधवः ।\nगच्छध्वमेनं शरणं शरण्यं कौरवर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava is father and mother of all beings; go to him for refuge, bulls of the Kurus, for he is the giver of refuge."}}]}]}